<title>POLAND: Polish construction rises 6.6 pct in September.</title>
<headline>Polish construction rises 6.6 pct in September.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish construction sales rose 6.6 percent in September, after a 3.0-percent rise in August and were 16.1-percent higher than in September 1995, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said.</p>
<p>Construction sales rose 3.9 percent in the first nine months of 1996, against a 13.8-percent rise in the same period in 1995.</p>
<p> POLISH CONSTRUCTION	 SEPTEMBER     AUGUST	 SEPT 1995</p>
<p> month/month pct change	 6.6	 3.0  (3.2)	 5.8</p>
<p> yr/yr pct change		16.1	15.2 (15.5)	13.3</p>
<p>NOTES: Revised data in brackets. September 1996 had 22 working days, while August 1996 and September 1995 had 23 working days. (*) 1992=100</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
